#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""wx-wallpaper - render the current weather onto the GNOME desktop background.

Ubuntu/GNOME (Wayland) gives you one reliable hook for the wallpaper:
    gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.background picture-uri(-dark) file://...
The shell reloads that image only when the *path* changes, so every render is
written to a fresh timestamped file. The HUD is composited on top of your normal
wallpaper, so the desktop still looks like your desktop.

    wx-wallpaper            fetch, render, apply
    wx-wallpaper --dry-run  render to a preview file, leave the desktop alone
    wx-wallpaper --status   show config + last render
"""

